\begin_layout Subsubsection
When Can the Next Streamer Start?
\begin_inset CommandInset label
LatexCommand label
name "sec:repro_next_streamer"

\end_inset

\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The first streamer started when the field at the tip reached the value given by 
\begin_inset Formula $27.5\,\text{kV}$
\end_inset
 without space charge, 
\begin_inset Formula $149.4\,\text{kV/cm}$
\end_inset
 (first row of 
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand formatted
reference "tab:repro_fig5_tip"
plural "false"
caps "false"
noprefix "false"
nolink "false"
tuple "list"

\end_inset
). The tip and the air are the same afterwards, so the next streamer needs the same tip field again. The difference is that the tip field now also contains the field of the space charge:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset Formula 
\begin{equation}
E_{total}(z=0,t)\ge149.4\,\text{kV/cm}.\label{eq:repro_second_streamer}
\end{equation}
\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
In our simulation this happens at 
\begin_inset Formula $t=3.25\,\mu\text{s}$
\end_inset
, when the voltage is 
\begin_inset Formula $51.4\,\text{kV}$
\end_inset
. The second streamer therefore needs almost twice the voltage of the first, because the charge left by the first streamer shields the tip. This is the space-charge effect the paper studies. The second streamer itself is modelled in Section 
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand ref
reference "sec:repro_fig678"
plural "false"
caps "false"
noprefix "false"
nolink "false"
tuple "list"

\end_inset
.
\end_layout

